hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3752","The leaves here should not be broken, nor should the (tree) here be cut, because the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has declared it a sanctuary. However, you may shake (the trees) gently."
"3753","If I live, in sha Allah, I shall certainly expel the Jews and Christians from the Arabian Peninsula. (Using translation from Aḥmad 215)"
"3754","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) performed Hajj while sitting on a saddle. He was not a miserly person, but he mentioned that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also went for Hajj riding on a saddle; that was his mount. (Zamilah refers to that she-camel on which luggage is loaded.)"
"3755","I am still seeing Sayyiduna Musa bin Imran (peace be upon him) descending on foot from the valley of Harsha."
"3756","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: A man stood before him and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! My name has been registered for participation in such-and-such battle, while my wife wants to set out for Hajj."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go and perform Hajj with your wife."
"3757","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Go and perform Hajj with your wife."
"3758","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for any woman to travel, except that her mahram is with her; in that case, the ruling is different."
"3759","""The people of Al-Madinah should enter into Ihram from Dhul-Hulaifah, the people of Ash-sham from Al-Juhfah, the people of Najd from Qarn."" 'Abdullah said: ""And it was conveyed to me, that the Messenger of Allah said: 'And the people of Yemen should enter into Ihram from Yalamlam.''' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2651)"
"3760","""The people of Al-Madinah should enter into Ihram from Dhul-Hulaifah, the people of Ash-sham from Al-Juhfah, the people of Najd from Qarn."" 'Abdullah said: ""And it was conveyed to me, that the Messenger of Allah said: 'And the people of Yemen should enter into Ihram from Yalamlam.''' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2651)"
"3761","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: A man addressed the Prophet (peace be upon him) in a loud voice and asked, \""What do you command us regarding from where we should enter into the state of Ihram?\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \""The people of Madinah will enter Ihram from Dhu'l-Hulayfah, the people of Sham from Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: People say that the Proph"
"3762","Ibn ʿUmar said this is your al-Baida’ about which you ascribe falsehood to the Messenger of Allah (SWAS). He did not raise his voice in talbiyah but from the masjid, i.e. the mosque of Dhu al-Hulaifah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1771)"
"3763","AbuAbdurRahman, I saw you doing things which I did not see being done by your companions. He asked: What are they, Ibn Jurayj? He replied: I saw you touching only the two Yamani corners; and I saw you wearing shoes having no hair; I saw you dyeing in yellow colour; and I saw you wearing ihram on the eighth of Dhul-Hijjah, whereas the people had worn ihram when they sighted the moon. Abdullah ibn Umar replied: As regards the corners, I have not seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touching anything (in the Ka'bah) but the two Yamani corners. As for the tanned leather shoes, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing tanned leather shoes, and he would wear them after ablution. Therefore I like to wear them. As regards wearing yellow, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing yellow, so I like to wear with it. As regards shouting the talbiyah, I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raising his voice in talbiyah when his she-camel stood up with him on its back. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1772)"
"3764","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed four Umrahs, all of which were in the month of Dhu al-Qi'dah. One Umrah was p"
"3765","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: By Allah! The Messenger of Allah did not perform Umrah in the month of Dhul-Hijjah so that he could end the tradition of the polytheists through it. The reason for this is that the Quraysh and the followers of their religion used to say: When the camel's hair grows long and the wound on its back heals (i.e., the wound that is caused by placing the saddle for the pilgrim), and the month of Safar begins, then it becomes permissibl"
"3766","ʿA’ishah said ; I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (SWAS) preparatory to his entering the sacred state before he put on Ihram, and preparatory to putting off Ihram before he made the circuits round the House (the Ka’bah). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1745)"
"3767","""It is as if I can see the glistening of the perfume on the head of the Messenger of Allah while he is in Ihram. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2695)"
"3768","I applied perfume to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) at the time when he assumed Ihram, and after three days had passed, I saw the trace of perfume in his hair parting, and he was still in the state of Ihram."
"3769","I still seem to see the glistening of the perfume where the hair was parted on the head of the Messenger of Allah (SWAS) while he was wearing Ihram. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1746)"
"3770","""'Aishah said: 'I put perfume on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he entered Ihram and on the Day of Sacrifice before he circumambulated the House, using perfume containing musk.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2692)"
"3771","I applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he entered upon the state of lhram and (concluding) before circumambulating the (sacred) House. (Using translation from Muslim 1189a)"
"3772","ʿA’ishah said ; I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (SWAS) preparatory to his entering the sacred state before he put on Ihram, and preparatory to putting off Ihram before he made the circuits round the House (the Ka’bah). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1745)"
"3773","I am unable to proceed further, there I will come out of Ihram."
"3774","I am unable to proceed further, there I will come out of Ihram."
"3775","I wish to perform Hajj and I am sick. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Enter into Ihram for Hajj and stipulate the condition that wherever I am unable to proceed further, I will come out of Ihram."
"3776","I made the same Ihram as the Messenger of Allah made."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If I had a sacrificial animal with me, I would have come out of Ihram."
"3777","I set out from Yemen. I intended that I would enter into Ihram with the same intention as the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I have entered into Ihram for both Hajj and Umrah together."
"3778","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) instructed him to take off the cloak and wash it two or three times. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Whatever you do in Hajj, do the same in Umrah (i.e., wear the Ihram in the same manner)."
"3779","The narrator states: Revelation began to descend upon the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). He was covered with a cloth. Sayyiduna Ya’la states: I wished that I could see the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) in the state when revelation was descending upon him. He narrates: Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) lifted the edge of the cloth and I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and he was snoring. When this state ended, he said: Where is the person who was asking about ‘Umrah? Wash off the yellow mark from yourself (the narrator is doubtful whether these are the words), wash off the fragrance, and take off your cloak, and in your ‘Umrah do what you do in Hajj (i.e., wear the same type of Ihram)."
"3780","Hammad bin Zaid narrates: I was sitting with Imam Abu Hanifa (may Allah have mercy on him) in Makkah when a person came to him and said: I wore socks during Ihram (the narrator is unsure if these are the exact words) or I wore trousers while I was in Ihram. This doubt is from the narrator named Ibrahim. So Imam Abu Hanifa (may Allah have mercy on him) said to him: You are required to offer a sacrifice (dam). Hammad bin Zaid says: I asked this person: Do you have shoes? Do you have an izar (waist cloth)? He replied: No, I do not. I said: O Abu Hanifa! This person says that he does not have those things. So Imam Abu Hanifa said: The ruling is the same whether he has them or not."
"3781","So I said: Amr bin Dinar narrated from Jabir bin Zaid, from Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""A person who does not have an izar (waist-wrapper) may wear trousers, and a person who does not have shoes may wear leather socks."
"3782","Ayub narrated from Nafi’ that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: “A person who does not find an izar (lower garment) may wear trousers, and a person who does not find shoes may wear socks.” The narrator says: Then he gestured with his hand, and Ibrahim bin Hajjaj gestured as if he did not care about the hadith, so I got up from him. Then Hajjaj bin Arta’ah met me inside the mosque, so I said: O Arta’ah, what do you say about a muhrim (person in ihram) who wears trousers or socks? He replied: Amr bin Dinar narrated from Jabir bin Zaid, from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “A person who does not find an izar may wear trousers, and a person who does not find shoes may wear socks.”"
"3783","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""A person may wear trousers if he does not find an izar (waist-wrapper),"
"3784","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and bl"
"3785","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""Whoever does not find an izar (lower garment), let him wear trousers, and whoever does not find shoes, let him wear leather socks (moza).\"""""
"3786","I heard the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon at ʿArafat saying, ""If a Muhrim does not find slippers, he could wear Khuffs (socks made from thick fabric or leather, but he has to cut short the Khuffs below the ankles), and if he does not find an Izar (a waist sheet for wrapping the lower half of the body) he could wear trousers."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1841)"
"3787","“Whoever does not have sandals let him wear leather socks, and let him cut them to below the ankle.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2932)"
"3788","That the Prophet said ""If a Muhrim cannot find sandals then let him wear Khuffs, and cut them, so that they come lower than the ankles.'' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2680)"
"3789","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Whoever cannot get an Izar, can wear trousers, and whoever cannot wear sandals can wear Khuffs (socks made from thick fabric or leather)."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5804)"
"3790","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, when he was in ‘Aqiq: “Someone came to me from my Lord and said: ‘Pray in this blessed valley and say: (I intend to do) ‘Umrah in Hajj.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2976)"
"3791","""We, the Companions of the Prophet, entered Ihram for Hajj only, and nothing else. We came to Makkah on the morning of the fourth of Dhul-Hajjah, and the Prophet commanded us: ""Exit Ihram and make it Umrah. He heard that we were saying: 'when there are only five days between us and 'Arafat he commands us to exit Ihram and we will go out to Mina with our male members dripping with semen (because of recent intimacy with our wives)?' the Prophet stood up and addressed us, saying: 'I have heard what you said. I am the most righteous and the most pious of you, and were it not for the Hadi I would have exited Ihram. If I had known what I know now, I would not have from Yemen and he said: 'for what did you enter Ihram?' He said: 'For that for which the Messenger of Allah entered Ihram.' Suraq bin Malik bin Jushum said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you think that this Umrah of ours is for this year only or for all time?' He said: 'It is for all time."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2805)"
"3792","Sayyidina Abdur Rahman bin Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) to take Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) to Tan'eem. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I entered into the state of Ihram for Umrah from there."
"3793","The narrator says: So we ended our Ihram and converted it into 'Umrah. When the morning of Tarwiyah came, we again began reciting the Talbiyah for Hajj and set out towards Mina."
"3794","""The Messenger of Allah came on the fourth day of Dhul-Hijjah having entered Ihram for Hajj. He prayed Subh in Al-Batha and said: 'Whoever wants to make it Umrah, let him do so.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2871)"
"3795","' Aisha said, ""We set out with Messenger of Allah ﷺs in the months of Hajj, and (in) the nights of Hajj, and at the time and places of Hajj and in a state of Hajj. We dismounted at Sarif (a village six miles from Mecca). The Prophet ﷺ then addressed his companions and said, ""Anyone who has not got the Hadi and likes to do Umra instead of Hajj may do so (i.e. Hajj-al-Tamattuʿ) and anyone who has got the Hadi should not finish the Ihram after performing ' ʿUmra). (i.e. Hajj-al-Qiran). Aisha added, ""The companions of the Prophet ﷺ obeyed the above (order) and some of them (i.e. who did not have Hadi) finished their Ihram after Umra."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ and some of his companions were resourceful and had the Hadi with them, they could not perform Umra (alone) (but had to perform both Hajj and Umra with one Ihram). Aisha added, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and saw me weeping and said, ""What makes you weep, O Hantah?"" I replied, ""I have heard your conversation with your companions and I cannot perform the Umra."" He asked, ""What is wrong with you?' I replied, ' I do not offer the prayers (i.e. I have my menses).' He said, ' It will not harm you for you are one of the daughters of Adam, and Allah has written for you (this state) as He has written it for them. Keep on with your intentions for Hajj and Allah may reward you that."" Aisha further added, ""Then we proceeded for Hajj till we reached Mina and I became clean from my menses. Then I went out from Mina and performed Tawaf round the Kaʿba."" Aisha added, ""I went along with the Prophet ﷺ in his final departure (from Hajj) till he dismounted at Al-Muhassab (a valley outside Mecca), and we too, dismounted with him."" He called ' ʿAbdur-Rahman bin Abu Bakr and said to him, ' Take your sister outside the sanctuary of Mecca and let her assume Ihram for ' ʿUmra, and when you had finished ' ʿUmra, return to this place and I will wait for you both till you both return to me.' "" ' Aisha added, "" So we went out of the sanctuary of Mecca and after finishing from the ' ʿUmra and the Tawaf we returned to the Prophet ﷺ at dawn. He said, 'Have you performed the ' ʿUmra?' We replied in the affirmative. So he announced the departure amongst his companions and the people set out for the journey, and the Prophet: too left for Medina.'' (Using translation from Bukhārī 1560)"
"3796","narrates: So we put on Ihram from Batha."
"3797","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) passed by a woman. It was said to her: This is the Messenger of Allah. So the woman took hold of the arm of her child who was with her. She said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Has this child performed Hajj? The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: Yes, and you will also have the reward (for it)."
"3798","I am the Messenger of Allah. The woman brought out her child and asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Has this child's Hajj been performed? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: (Yes,) and you will also receive the reward."
"3799","Ibn ‘Umar said Talbiyah uttered by the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ was Labbaik(always ready to obey), O Allaah labbaik, labbaik; Thou hast no partner, praise and grace are Thine, and the Dominion, Thou hast no partner. The narrator said ‘Abd Allaah bin ‘Umar used to add to his talbiyah Labbaik, labbaik, labbaik wa sa’daik(give me blessing after blessing) and good is Thy hands, desire and actions are directed towards Thee. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1812)"
"3800","“Labbaika ilahal-haqq, labbaika (Here I am, O god of Truth, here I am).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2920)"
"3801","I am seeing right now Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him). Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the length of his hair and his complexion (and said): He has placed both his fingers in both his ears and, reciting the words of Talbiyah, is passing through this valley beseeching Allah Almighty. The narrator says: Then we moved ahead from this valley and we came—Dawud, the narrator, has mentioned this—I think these words are in the narration: We came to the pass called Harsha. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Which pass is this? We replied: This is the Harsha pass. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is as if I am seeing right now Sayyiduna Yunus (peace be upon him), riding his red camel, whose bridle is made of palm fibers. He is wearing a woolen cloak and, passing through this pass, is reciting the Talbiyah in a loud voice."
"3802","“Jibra’il came to me and told me to command my Companions to raise their voices when reciting the Talbiyah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2922)"
"3803","“Jibril came to me and said: ‘O Muhammad! Tell your Companions to raise their voices when reciting the Talbiyah, for it is one of the symbols of Hajj.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2923)"
"3804","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) seated Sayyiduna Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) behind him while"
"3805","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the Conquest, with a helmet on his head. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2805)"
"3806","On the day of the Conquest, the Prophet ﷺ entered Mecca, wearing a helmet on his head. When he took it off, a man came and said, ""Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtain of the Kaʿba."" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Kill him."" (Malik a sub-narrator said, ""On that day the Prophet ﷺ was not in a state of Ihram as it appeared to us, and Allah knows better."") (Using translation from Bukhārī 4286)"
"3807","In the year of the conquest of Mecca, the Prophet ﷺ entered Mecca from Kada' at the higher place of Mecca. (Hisham, a sub-narrator said, "" ʿUrwa used to enter (Mecca) from both Kada' and Kuda and he often entered through Kada' which was nearer to his dwelling place.)"" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1579)"
"3808","narrates: A man from Iraq said: Ask Urwah bin Zubair about a person who enters into the state of Ihram for Hajj and performs the Tawaf of the House of Allah; should he continue reciting the Talbiyah or not? So Urwah informed that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed Hajj. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) has reported that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) arrived in Makkah, the very first thing he did was perform ablution and then performed the Tawaf of the House of Allah."
"3809","""When the Messenger of Allah arrived in Makkah he circumambulated the House seven times, then he prayed two Rakahs behind the Maqam. Then, he went out to As-Safa through the gate that is usually used to exit, and performed Sai between As-Safa and Al-Marwah."" (One of the narrators Shubah said: Ayub informed me from Amr bin Dinar from Ibn Umar that he said: ""A Sunnah."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2966)"
"3810","Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: ""When the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, came to Makkah, he performed ramal (brisk walking) while performing tawaf."
"3811","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). I said: O Ibn Abbas, individuals from your peopl"
"3812","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas abo"
"3813","Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: ""The Pr"
"3814","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: On the occasion of ‘Umrah after Hudaybiyyah, when the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) were about to enter Makkah, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to his companions: “Tomorrow, people will see you, so you should appear strong.” When these people entered the mosque, they performed istilam of the Black Stone, then they performed raml. The Prophet (peace be upon him) was also with them, until they reached the Yeme"
"3815","(The wife of the Prophet) Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Don't you see that when your people built the Kaʿba, they did not build it on all Abraham's foundations?"" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Why don't you rebuild it on Abraham's foundations?"" He said, ""Were your people not so close to (the period of Heathenism, i.e. the Period between their being Muslims and being infidels), I would do so."" The sub-narrator, ʿAbdullah bin ʿUmar said, ""Aisha had surely heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying that, for I do not think that Messenger of Allah ﷺ left touching the two corners of the Kaʿba facing Al-Hijr except because the Kaʿba was not built on all Abraham's foundations."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 4484)"
"3816","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: O Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), if your people had not recently left the Age of Ignorance, I would have had the House of Allah (the Ka'bah) demolished and included in it the part that they had left out, which is the Hatim. Their funds had run short, so they joined it with the ground, and I would have rebuilt it according to the foundations of our master Ibrahim (peace be upon him). I would have made two doors for it: one door on the eastern side and one on the western side. The narrator states: For this reason, Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) had it demolished and rebuilt."
"3817","Aswad reports: Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) asked Aswad—he used to visit Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and she showed him special affection. Aswad narrated: Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) informed that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If your people had not recently left the Age of Ignorance, I would have demolished the Ka'bah and built two doors for it."" The narrator says: That is why Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) had it demolished and built two doors for it."
"3818","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: O Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)! If your people were not so close to the time of ignorance, I would have demolished the Ka'bah and added six handspans of Hatim into it, because the Quraysh had left out this part when they built it, and I would have made two doors for it, one eastern door and one western door, and I would have placed its doors level with the ground."
"3819","Jabir b. 'Abdullah reported that Allah's Apostle ﷺ and his Companions did not observe Sa'i between al-Safa' and al-Marwa but only one Sa'i. (Using translation from Muslim 1279a)"
"3820","The narrator says: I asked my father, “What announcement did you people make?” So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: We were saying, “After this year, no polytheist will perform Hajj,” so after that year, no polytheist performed Hajj, “and no naked person will circumambulate the House of Allah, and only a believer will enter Paradise. And whoever has a treaty with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a certain period, its duration is four months. When four months have passed, then Allah and His Messenger are free from obligations to the polytheists.” So the polytheists, mocking this, were saying: “No, one month is enough.”"
"3821","I know that you are only a stone. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you, I would not have kissed you. (Using translation from Aḥmad 226)"
"3822","I know that you are only a stone. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you, I would not have kissed you. (Using translation from Aḥmad 226)"
"3823","I replied: I performed its Istilam and then left it. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You did right."
"3824","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) kissing it, I have never abandoned this practice."
"3825","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Tawaf while riding his camel. When we came opposite the Black Stone, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed towards it."
"3826","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say between the two corners: O Allah, bring us a blessing in this world and a blessing in the next and guard us from punishment of Hell. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1892)"
"3827","Ibn ‘Umar said I have not seen the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ touching anything in the House (the Ka’bah) but the two Yamani corners. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1874)"
"3828","I say this, and I seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty for myself and for you."
"3829","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Tawaf of the Ka'bah while riding his camel, and he touched the Black Stone (Hajar al-Aswad) with his staff."
"3830","I did so."
"3831","While performing the Tawaf around the Kaʿba, the Prophet ﷺ passed by a person leading another person by a hair-rope nose-ring in his nose. The Prophet ﷺ cut the hair-rope nose-ring off with his hand and ordered the man to lead him by the hand. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6703)"
"3832","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) cut it and said: You (hold his hand and take him along)."
"3833","Umm Salamah said I complained to the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ that I was ill. He said “Perform the circumambulation riding behind the people”. She said “I performed circumambulation and the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ was praying towards the side of the House(the Ka’bah) and reciting “by al Tur and a Book inscribed”.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1882)"
"3834","Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: We set out with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and our intention was only to perform Hajj. When we reached the place of Sarif, I began menstruating. The Prophet (peace be upon him) came to me and I was crying. He asked: What has happened to you, have you started menstruating? I replied: Yes. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: This is a thing which Allah has ordained for the daughters of Adam. You should do all the rituals that a pilgrim does, except that you should not perform the Tawaf of the House (Ka'bah). Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives."
"3835","Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I came to Makkah while I was menstruating. I did not perform the Tawaf of the House (Ka'bah) nor the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. I complained about this to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Do all the acts that a pilgrim does, except do not perform the Tawaf of the House until you become pure."
"3836","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Circumambulating the House of Allah (the Ka'bah) is also like performing prayer, except that Allah the Exalted has permitted talking during it. So whoever speaks (while performing tawaf), he should only speak good words."
"3837","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) drank Zamzam water during Tawaf."
"3838","I served. (water of) Zamzam to Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he drank it while standing. (Using translation from Muslim 2027a)"
"3839","I said to ʿAisha, the wife of the Prophet, and I was at that time a young boy, ""How do you interpret the Statement of Allah: ""Verily, Safa and Marwa (i.e. two mountains at Mecca) are among the Symbols of Allah."" So it is not harmful of those who perform the Hajj to the House of Allah) or perform the Umra, to ambulate (Tawaf) between them. In my opinion it is not sinful for one not to ambulate (Tawaf) between them."" ʿAisha said, ""Your interpretation is wrong for as you say, the Verse should have been: ""So it is not harmful of those who perform the Hajj or Umra to the House, not to ambulate (Tawaf) between them.' This Verse was revealed in connection with the Ansar who (during the Pre-Islamic Period) used to visit Manat (i.e. an idol) after assuming their Ihram, and it was situated near Qudaid (i.e. a place at Mecca), and they used to regard it sinful to ambulate between Safa and Marwa after embracing Islam. When Islam came, they asked Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, whereupon Allah revealed:-- ""Verily, Safa and Marwa (i.e. two mountains at Mecca) are among the Symbols of Allah. So it is not harmful of those who perform the Hajj of the House (of Allah) or perform the Umra, to ambulate (Tawaf) between them."" (2.158) (Using translation from Bukhārī 4495)"
"3840","I asked the noble wife of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): I said to her: What is your opinion about the statement of Allah Almighty? ""Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no sin upon him if he walks between them."" I think that if someone does not perform the Sa'i between them, there is no harm upon him. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Absolutely not, if it were as you say, then the verse would have been: ""There is no sin upon him who does not walk between them."" (Then Lady Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, explained:) This verse was revealed about some of the Ansar who used to assume Ihram for Manat (an idol). They felt it was wrong to perform Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. When Islam came, people asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) about this, so Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no sin upon him if he walks between them. And whoever does good voluntarily, then indeed, Allah is Appreciative and Knowing."" Urwah bin Zubair narrates: I asked the noble wife of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): I said to her: What is your opinion about the statement of Allah Almighty? ""Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah,"" this verse until its end. I said to Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): By Allah! There is no sin upon the one who does not perform the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. So Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O my nephew! You have said a very wrong thing about this verse. If it meant what you are saying, then the verse should have been: ""There is no sin upon him if he does not walk between them."" In fact, this verse was revealed about the Ansar who, before accepting Islam, used to assume Ihram in the name of Manat, the false deity. These people used to worship it near Mushallal. Whoever assumed Ihram in its name considered it a sin to perform the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. When people asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) about this, they said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! We used to consider it a sin to perform the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. So Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no sin upon him if he walks between them."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) declared the Sa'i between them as Sunnah, so now it is not permissible for anyone to abandon the Sa'i between them. Zuhri says: I took this narration to Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman, the narration which Urwah narrated to me from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman said: This is indeed knowledge; I had not heard this before. I had previously heard some scholars say that everyone used to perform the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, except those whom Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned, who used to take sacrificial animals in the name of Manat. When Allah Almighty mentioned the Tawaf of the House in the Qur'an and did not mention the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah (people became confused about this), so Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no sin upon him if he walks between them."" Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman said: So I heard that this verse was revealed about both groups: those who, in the time of ignorance, used to perform the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, so they considered it a sin in Islam, thinking that Allah Almighty has commanded us to perform Tawaf of the House and has not mentioned Safa and Marwah. This was at the time when Allah Almighty had only mentioned the Tawaf of the House."
"3841","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): Your people say that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ramal and that this is Sunnah. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: They have stated some things correctly and some things incorrectly. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, the polytheists were present at Qaiqan. They were talking among themselves, mocking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions (saying that they are weak people). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ramal and ordered his companions to do ramal as well. (Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) This is not Sunnah."
"3842","when the Messenger of Allah stood on top of As-Safa, he recited the Takbir three times and said: ""La ilaha illallah, Wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu, yuhyi wa yumitu, wa huwaala kulli shayin qadir (There is none worthy of worship except Allah alone with no partner or associate, His is the dominion and to Him be praise, He gives life and death, and He has power over all things)."" He did three times, and supplicated, and did the same a top Al-Marwah. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2972)"
"3843","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) supplicating against the (enemy) armies in this way: “O Allah! Defeat them, make them stumble. O Revealer of the Book, O Swift in reckoning, defeat the (enemy) armies. O Allah! Defeat them.”"
"3844","""I heard him saying"" - meaning the Prophet ﷺ - ""while supplicating against the Ahzab: 'O Allah, Revealer of Book! Severe is reckoning! Rout the Ahzab and shake them.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1678)"
"3845","I said to Ibn ʿAbbas (Allah be pleased with them): Do you think that walking swiftly round the House in three circuits, and just walking in four circuits is the Sunnah (of the Holy Prophet), for your people say that it is Sunnah? Thereupon he (Ibn ʿAbbas) said: They have told the truth and the lie (too). I said: What do your words ""They have told the truth and the lie (too)"" imply? Thereupon he said: Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Mecca and the polytheists said that Muhammad and his Companions had emaciated and would, therefore, be unable to circumambulate the House; and they felt jealous of him (the Holy Prophet). (It was due to this) that Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to walk swiftly in three (circuits) and walk (normally) in four. I said to him: Inform me if it is Sunnah to observe Tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwa while riding, for your people look upon it as Sunnah. He (Ibn ʿAbbas) said: They have told the truth and the lie too. I said: What do your words ""They have told the truth and the lie too"" imply? He said: When Messenger of Allah ﷺ had come to Mecca, there was such a large gathering of people around him that even the virgins had come out of their houses (to catch a glimpse of his face). And they were saying: He is Muhammad; He is Muhammad. Messenger of Allah ﷺ (was so gentle and kind) that the people were not beaten back (to make way) in front of him. When there was a throng (of people) around him, he rode (the she-camel). However, walking and trotting are better. (Using translation from Muslim 1264a)"
"3846","""I asked anas bin Malik: 'Tell me of something that you learned from the Messenger of Allah; where did he pray Zuhr on the day of At-Tarwiyah?' He said: 'In Mina.' I said: 'Where did he pray Asr on the day of An-Nafr?' He said: 'In Al-Abtah.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2997)"
"3847","I asked Anas bin Malik while we were proceeding from Mina to ʿArafat, ""What do you use to do on this day when you were with Messenger of Allah ﷺ ?"" Anas said, ""Some of us used to recite Talbiya and nobody objected to that, and others used to recite Takbir and nobody objected to that."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1659)"
"3848","narrator is unsure about a word here). The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""What day is it today?"" We remained silent, thinking perhaps he would give it a name other than its usual one. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Is it not the Day of Sacrifice?"" We replied: ""Yes."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""What month is this?"" We remained silent, thinking perhaps he would give it another name. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Is it not Dhul-Hijjah?"" We replied: ""Yes."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""What city is this?"" We remained silent, thinking perhaps he would give it another name. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""Is it not the sacred city?"" We replied: ""Yes!"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your lives, your wealth, and your honor are as sacred to one another as this day is in this month in this city. Beware! Let every present person convey this message to the absent, for it may be that the one to whom it is conveyed will preserve it better than the one who heard it."
"3849","I came to Arafah. There I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing with the people at Arafah. I said: By Allah! He belongs to the Hums (the Quraysh), why is he standing here?"
"3850","""I came to the Prophet in Jam (Al-Muzdalifah) and said: 'Is there Hajj for me?' He said: 'Whoever offers this prayer with us and observed this standing until he departed, and he departed before that from Arafat by night or by day, then his Hajj is complete. And he has completed the prescribed duties.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3042)"
"3851","""I saw the Messenger of Allah stading in Al-Muzdalifah and he said: 'Whoever offers this prayer whith us here then stands with us and stood before that in Arafat by nightor by day, his Hajj is complete. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3039)"
"3852","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, Allah expresses pride before the inhabitants of the heavens, that is, the angels, regarding the people of Arafat and says: Look at My servants! They have come to Me, that is, to My court, disheveled and dust-covered."
"3853","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""There are no days more virtuous in the sight of Allah than the ten of Dhū al-Ḥijjah."" A man asked: O Messenger of Allah, are they more virtuous or the count of days fighting in the cause of Allah? He said, ""They are more virtuous than the count of days fighting in cause of Allah,"""",""... and there is no day more virtuous in the sight of Allah than the Day of ʿArafah: for He descends to the worldly sky and boasts about the people of earth to those in the sky and He says: 'Look at My servants appearing disheveled and dusty. They have come from every far corner ˹of earth˺ seeking my Mercy and they do not see my punishment.' You will not see more ˹people˺ having salvation from the Hellfire than the Day of ʿArafah.'"""
"3854","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “All of ‘Arafat is a place for standing (Wuquf), so keep yourselves above (away from) ‘Urnah. And all of Muzdalifah is a place for standing, so keep yourselves above (away from) Muhassir. Every path of Mina is a place for sacrifice, and sacrifice can be done on all the days of Tashreeq.”"
"3855","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to recite « » during the halt. He continued to mention the greatness of Allah Almighty and supplicated to Him. When he set out, the people had already departed, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them in a loud voice to proceed calmly. When he reached the valley, he poured water and performed ablution, then mounted again. When he arrived at Muzdalifah, he performed the Maghrib and Isha prayers together. When he had performed the Fajr prayer, he remained there. When he set out, the people also set out. When the people set out, he said: Proceed calmly. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was also pulling the reins of his mount, until when he entered the lower part of Mina, he said: It is obligatory upon you to pick such pebbles as can be held between the fingers; they will be thrown at the Jamrah. And at that place, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to recite the Talbiyah until he had performed the Rami of the Jamrah."
"3856","The Quraysh were the custodians of the House of Allah; they used to depart from Mina, while other people would depart from Arafat. So Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""You should also return from where the people return."
"3857","The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ returned from ‘Arafah. When he came to the mountain path , he alighted, urinated and performed the ablution, but he did not perform it completely. I said to him Prayer? He said “The prayer will be offered ahead of you.” He then mounted. When he reached Al Muzdalifah he alighted performed the ablution, performed it well. Thereafter iqamah for the prayer was called and he offered the sunset prayer. Then everyone made his Camel kneel down at his place. Iqamah was then called for night prayer and he offered it but he did not pray between them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1925)"
"3858","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Yazid that Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari told him, that during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ Maghrib and 'Isha' prayers together at Al-Muzdalifah. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 605)"
"3859","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) had led the people in prayer at this place in the same manner."
"3860","The Arabs in the pre-Islamic period did not return from al-Muzdalifah till they saw sunlight at the mountain Thabir. The Prophet ﷺ opposed them and returned before the sunrise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1938)"
"3861","I wished that I had also sought permission from him."
"3862","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) sent me along with those people who had been sent from Muzdalifah (before others) at night."
"3863","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: The Messenger of Allah sent me from Muzdalifah at night."""
"3864","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I wish that I had also taken permission from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) in the same way as Lady Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) did, and I would have performed the Fajr prayer in Mina and stoned the Jamrah before the people arrived. The narrator says: I asked Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): Did Lady Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) take permission from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)? She replied: Yes, she was a heavyset woman, so she asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) for permission, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) granted her permission."
"3865","Ibn ‘Abbas said I was among the weak members of his family whom the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ sent ahead on the night of Al Muzdalifah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1939)"
